const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does a new radiator cost on the Wirral?', a: 'A standard double panel radiator supplied and fitted is from £245 including VAT. Five radiators are from £1,195. Fitting one you bought is from £95. Designer and column radiators are from £250 to fit.' },
  { q: 'Do you cover all Wirral CH postcodes?', a: 'Yes. We cover CH41 to CH64, from Birkenhead, Wallasey and New Brighton to Hoylake, West Kirby, Heswall, Bebington, Bromborough and Neston. Prices are the same everywhere, with no call-out fee.' },
  { q: 'Can you fit column radiators in a Victorian house in Birkenhead or West Kirby?', a: 'Yes. Column radiators suit the high ceilings in Birkenhead, Wallasey, Hoylake and West Kirby. We work out the heat the room needs first, then pick the height and number of columns. Styles up to 1800mm tall are available.' },
  { q: 'My front room has a bay window and never gets warm. Why?', a: 'Often the radiator is on a side wall, or it is too small for the room. A radiator sized right and fitted under the bay heats the cold air from the glass. We check the size and position when we visit.' },
  { q: 'Can you add a radiator to a house with microbore pipes?', a: 'Yes. Many 1970s and 1980s homes in Prenton, Moreton and Bebington have thin microbore pipes. We use the right fittings and check the pipes and pump can carry the extra radiator first.' },
  { q: 'Is balancing included?', a: 'Yes, on every job. Balancing sets each radiator so the whole house heats evenly. Without it, a new radiator can starve the others of heat.' },
  { q: 'How long does it take to fit a radiator?', a: 'A straight swap takes 1 to 2 hours. A move takes 3 to 4 hours. Five radiators are usually done in one day.' },
  { q: 'How much is a radiator repair?', a: 'Repairs are charged by time. The first hour is £120 on weekdays 9am to 4pm, £150 evenings, nights and weekends, and £180 on bank holidays. There is no call-out fee.' },
  { q: 'Why is my radiator cold at the bottom?', a: 'Usually sludge has settled in it. Bleeding will not fix it. One radiator may need a flush. If several are cold at the bottom, the system needs a power flush.' },
  { q: 'Are you Gas Safe registered?', a: 'Yes. Radiator work on the heating circuit is done by our Gas Safe registered engineers. You can check any engineer on the Gas Safe Register.' },
];
